WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
Act 1.

2
00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.810
A council chamber, late at night.

3
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.350
A general walks in among the senators.

4
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.910
The Duke greets him: "Valiant Othello,
we must straight employ you" Earlier that

5
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.570
same night, in a dark street, two
figures shouted up at a lit window,

6
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.300
about the same man.

7
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.790
What were they saying?

8
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.720
So does Venice ever really accept him?

9
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.930
In this mission, you'll learn what the
word Moor meant to Shakespeare's audience,

10
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.360
and how he changed his source story.

11
00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:32.610
You'll look closely at what
Iago shouts up at that window,

12
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.290
and ask why he chooses those words.

13
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.800
And you'll track how Othello's view
of himself shifts as the play goes on.

14
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.630
Your mission: decide whether
Venice ever accepts him.
